  "internal_thinking": "I currently have 4 victory points and need one more settlement to win. My target is node 23, which is already connected to my road network. To build a settlement there, I need 1 Wood, 1 Brick, 1 Wheat, and 1 Sheep. After the dice roll of 4, I received 1 Wood (from Hex 3) and 1 Sheep (from Hex 12), bringing my total resources to 2 Wood, 2 Wheat, and 1 Sheep. I am exactly 1 Brick short of winning. However, looking at the current player resources, Shon has 2 Sheep and 1 Wheat, and Ziv has 1 Sheep. Neither of them has the Brick I need. I also tried to trade with Shon last turn and he confirmed he has no Brick. Since I only have 5 resources total and my best port is a 3:1 port at node 9, I cannot trade with the bank to get the Brick (I would need 3 of one resource to get 1 Brick, which would leave me with only 3 resources, but a settlement costs 4). There are no other legal moves I can make this turn that would bring me closer to winning or improve my position significantly. I will end my turn and hope for a 6 (Brick) or a trade opportunity next round. I will use the chat to downplay my position and deflect Ziv's pressure.",
  "note_to_self": "I am at 4 VP and only need 1 Brick to build a settlement at node 23 and win. Neither Shon nor Ziv has Brick right now. I need to watch for a 6 or 10 roll, or wait for them to collect resources I can trade for.",
